Interior dusk, the storm is just brewing on the horizon
A huge burning cauldron of oil hangs from the ceiling in a great hall, acting as a chandelier.
Below, a feast is being held
The wind howls outside, and the torches on the wall begin to dim.
The fire in the great hearth at the end of the hall, dims and goes out
The fire in the cauldron goes out,
The people at the feast begin to get up and look around nervously
light from the high windows around the ceiling barely break the shadow in the room
Without the flames, you can see a skeleton hanging by from it's wrists by two great chains.
The skeleton's toes barely dip into the cauldron, which is strung up by chains from the skeletons' hip
CLOSE UP SHOT OF THE SKELETON, THE FEAST CAN BE SEEN IN THE BACKGROUND BELOW
The master of the hall looks up at the skeleton and stands up from his chair, alarmed.
He grabs the shoulder of the woman next to him, and whispers in her ear.
Blood begins sweating from the bones.
The master of the hall, walks out of the room with the woman, and people begin get up from their seats, confused.
Sinew, muscle and skin is forming around the leaking blood vessels.
The hound (partially formed) opens his eyes.
The hound flexes his iron bound hands, and looks around the room, then up.
The feast-goers are leaving the hall in a panic
WIDE SHOT SHOWING THE ENTIRE HALL WITH THE HOUND AT THE CENTER
Hand over hand, the hound begins to lurch his way up one of the chains.
The giant cauldron sloshes as he climbs, scalding oil spills on people below.
Soldiers rush into the room from every door.
Two giant sentry statues crawl through the huge front gate, then stand, hunched against the 100 foot arched ceiling.
They reach for the Hound, but he has already reached the top.
He lets go and is ripped downwards by the cauldron, the chains whistle as they unfurl
With a deafening crack, the chains snap taught, between the hounds wrists, and the iron ceiling mounts.
The ceiling mounts give out, and the cauldron crashes through the table, and rolls across the room with the hound inside.
The soldiers and sentries close in around it
The hound crawls out of the oil, horrid burns covering every inch of his body, the chains drag behind his wrists
He sits up, and rips the chain binding him to the cauldron, out from where his flesh grew around it.
A sentry drives its' spear through his chest, and deep into the floor
With lightning speed, the hound grips the haft of the spear and pulls his skewered body up along its' length
